      <div class="person"><h4>B. Daniel – A Hybrid Software Developer</h4><p>My company introduced a hybrid schedule last year. I work from home three days a week and attend the office twice a week. I find this arrangement ideal because I can concentrate on complicated programming tasks at home, while office days give me opportunities to exchange ideas and solve problems with other developers.</p></div>
      <div class="person"><h4>C. Sophie – A Traditional Office Manager</h4><p>I have worked in a traditional office for more than ten years. I appreciate being able to communicate with my staff directly, especially when urgent decisions need to be made. Although I understand why some people prefer working from home, I believe certain management responsibilities are easier to handle when everyone is physically present.</p></div>
      <div class="person"><h4>D. Michael – A Freelance Graphic Designer</h4><p>I work independently and choose my own projects. This gives me considerable freedom, but it also means that my income is not always predictable. Some months are financially successful, while others are much quieter. Therefore, I have learned to manage my savings carefully and plan my expenses in advance.</p></div>
    `},
